From e7e123abf1bf5a369f2a85f75e90a196c3aa25bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cortex Security Patch <cortex-agent@local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:09:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(security): cached scan pass, per-host group visibility,
 sandbox drift demo

Phase Sec-3 -- follows directly on Phase Sec-2's security group
snapshots, drift detection, and REST panel commit.

Backend
- Add security_finding_cache + security_scan_runs tables
  (models.SecurityFindingCache / SecurityScanRun) and a periodic
  background pass (services/security_scan_cache.py, wired into main.py
  as SECURITY_SCAN_INTERVAL_SECONDS, default 45s) that does the Security
  Agent's four sub-checks per node on a schedule instead of live on every
  request. This is what was making /security and
  /security/security-groups block on a fresh Loki/Neutron/CVE-feed/eBPF
  round trip per host on every page load.
- routers/security.py: GET /findings, /findings/{hostname},
  /groups/{hostname} now read that cache (falling back to one live scan
  only for a host the periodic pass hasn't reached yet). New GET /health
  (scan-run history, mirrors GET /topology/health) and POST /resync
  (manual on-demand trigger, mirrors POST /topology/resync).
- New services/security_sandbox.py + POST|DELETE
  /security/sandbox/drift/{hostname} (admin-only, CORTEX_ENV=sandbox
  only): wraps openstack-sim's existing sandbox fault-injection
  endpoints into one call that takes a baseline snapshot, injects one
  real non-risky ingress rule, and re-scans the host immediately --
  turns the manual scripts/run_security_snapshot.py + curl walkthrough
  into a clickable drift demo.

Frontend
- New SecurityHealthBadge / SecurityRescanButton components (same
  pattern as TopologyHealthBadge / TopologyResyncButton) added to
  /security, /security/security-groups, and the per-host detail page --
  a scanned Xm ago badge plus a manual rescan trigger, alongside the
  existing cache-only Refresh button.
- Security groups list + detail pages now render the full
  current-groups-per-node listing (sec_group_signal.data.security_groups,
  already computed by security_audit.py but never surfaced) with each
  group flagged Clean/Flagged against that host own risky_rules/drift,
  instead of only ever showing aggregate counts.
- Detail page: added an explanation of what Drift since last snapshot
  means, plus a sandbox-only Simulate drift panel (only rendered when
  GET /security/status reports sandbox_mode) that injects and can remove
  one real demo rule via the new sandbox endpoints above.

infra/docker-compose.sandbox.yml: SECURITY_SCAN_INTERVAL_SECONDS=20 and
an explicit OPENSTACK_SIM_BASE_URL for the sandbox drift demo.
